WRONG PAIRING: a coordinator was given a bare key, not a descriptor.␀␀␀these keys are on a different network. switch it in SETTINGS > SIGNER.␀␀your coordinator sent no key information. pair it again, then rebuild.␀␀SIGN␀␀␀␀TOTAL LEAVING␀␀␀DUST ATTACK: spending it links your keys to a stranger. deselect it with coin control.␀␀CHANGE OUT OF REACH: your coordinator must rescan to see it.␀␀␀␀HIGH FEE: a big slice of what you send. lower it in your coordinator.␀␀␀INPUTS LINKED: shows %u of your addresses share one owner. use fewer coins.␀WHY FLAGGED␀TINY CHANGE: leaves a dust sized input behind. adjust the amount.␀␀␀ask your coordinator for the full previous transactions.␀␀␀␀CHANGE␀␀Whole coins get spent, so the rest returns.␀BACK TO YOU␀Keep a little in it and hand it over.␀␀␀HAND IT OVER␀␀␀␀Your coordinator set the rate. Higher rates go first.␀␀␀FEE RATE␀␀␀␀Where the fee comes from.␀␀␀SATS PER VBYTE␀␀THE FEE␀What you pay to get this payment mined.␀PAID TO MINERS␀␀A short code that names your keys. Your coordinator shows the same one.␀NAMES YOUR KEYS␀It picks which keys open, real or decoy.␀␀␀␀Which keys your seed words open. Your coordinator must use the same one.␀␀␀␀DERIVATION PATH Â· BIP84␀␀␀␀WHICH KEYS OPEN␀A payment your coordinator built for you.␀␀␀NOT SIGNED YET␀␀From coin flips, dice or the camera.␀␀␀␀NOBODY CAN GUESS␀␀␀␀Seed words that rebuild your keys. Any BIP39 compatible signer opens them.␀␀WRITE THEM DOWN␀PAIRING sends this as a QR. Nobody types it.␀␀␀␀The whole thing.␀␀␀␀It lets your coordinator see your coins. It cannot spend them.␀␀12 WORDS␀␀␀␀most seed words come in twelve␀␀24 WORDS␀␀␀␀choose it to match the seed words you have␀␀AMNESIC␀load your seed words every session␀␀NOTHING LEAVES THIS DEVICE␀␀anyone can spend these␀␀NOT A BLIND DRAW␀␀␀␀a thief tries that part␀all from one part of the list.␀␀fewer real choices␀␀some seed words came up more than once.␀cut up, mix, draw blind␀THE LIST: the same 2048 words everywhere. it is public.
YOUR DRAW: cut it up, or print BIP39 tiles, mix them in a jar and take 11 unseen.
THE LAST WORD: the device works it out. it is a checksum, not a choice.␀␀␀THE 2048 WORD LIST␀␀you cut up a word list and draw blind.␀␀one short run, typed over and over.␀any one of these completes your seed words.␀PICK THE LAST WORD␀␀your draw. the signer finds only the last word.␀every word here is the same word.␀␀␀far easier to guess␀your seed words are in list order.␀␀BLIND DRAW␀␀cut up the list, draw 11␀␀␀␀HOW IT WORKS␀␀␀␀chosen is never random␀␀THE RISK␀␀␀␀CHECK YOUR SEED WORDS␀␀␀a word is wrong or out of order.
check your paper and try again.␀␀␀␀that is not a valid set of BIP39 seed words␀DICE␀␀␀␀CAMERA AND TAPS␀NEW SEED WORDS␀␀RESTORE SEED WORDS␀␀%d of 2048 words fit yours␀␀your last word is math, not chance.␀THE BUILT IN CHECK␀␀worked out, not chosen␀␀WHAT IT IS␀␀one word copied wrong␀␀␀IT CATCHES␀␀HEADS␀␀␀you flip a coin 128 times.␀␀your seed words come only from these flips.␀FLIP A COIN␀TAILS␀␀␀heads 0 tails 1, SHA256. check on any computer.␀YOURS, NOT ITS: the randomness is your own hand, not this signer's word.
WHAT GETS REFUSED: entries that lean one way, or run in order.
NOTHING IS LOST: what you entered is kept. keep going.␀␀WHY YOU DO THIS BY HAND␀you roll a die 50 times.␀␀␀␀PATTERN␀these run in order. chance does not.␀␀␀␀your seed words come only from these rolls.␀ROLL A DIE␀␀UNDO␀␀␀␀UNEVEN␀␀some faces came up far more than the rest␀␀␀your rolls, then SHA256. check on any computer.␀a key someone can guess␀nothing lost, keep going␀␀␀␀THE FIX␀CHECK WHAT YOU ENTERED␀␀ADD YOUR TAPS␀␀␀source 1 done.␀␀the sources did not combine, so nothing was saved. you had no keys yet, so nothing was lost.␀␀␀␀NO SEED WORDS MADE␀␀good. keep it there.␀␀␀␀too dark or too plain. point somewhere busier.␀␀WHAT YOU POINT AT: the scene in front of the lens.
THE CHIP ITSELF: hardware noise, on since boot.
YOUR OWN HANDS: the exact moment of each tap.
THE TIMING INSIDE: tiny delays as this board works.
STILL NOT SURE: use DICE and check it yourself.␀␀␀␀one bad source cannot decide your keys.␀WHY FOUR SOURCES␀␀␀␀SOURCE 1   WHAT YOU POINT AT␀␀␀␀not a blank wall. gravel, leaves, a deck.␀␀␀SOURCE 2   THE CHIP ITSELF␀␀hardware noise, always running.␀SOURCE 3   YOUR OWN HANDS␀␀␀the view is frozen. move the camera.␀␀␀␀tap anywhere in here. any rhythm.␀␀␀your timing is the part no manufacturer can guess.␀␀TAP TO ADD RANDOMNESS␀␀␀saved here encrypted. your passphrase guards your real keys, and is never saved here.␀␀␀WHOEVER READS THESE CAN SPEND THE COINS␀SLIDE TO SHOW␀␀␀how many seed words?␀␀␀␀unencrypted. your passphrase is not here␀␀␀␀this signer does not speak that backup's mode, or it is damaged.␀␀␀␀this signer cannot open it␀␀BACKUP NOT OPENED␀␀␀no .kef backup files on this card.␀␀insert the card that holds the .kef backup, then try again.␀pick the one to open␀␀␀␀BACKUPS ON THE CARD␀nothing is saved on this device␀a backup only your password opens␀␀␀LOAD YOUR SEED WORDS␀␀␀␀type the seed words from your paper.␀␀␀␀MADE WITH␀␀␀brought in from another device.␀made before this signer kept a record.␀␀NOT RECORDED␀␀␀␀HOW YOUR KEYS WERE MADE␀50 rolls or 128 flips, in one go␀␀␀␀DICE OR COIN␀␀␀␀how should the seed words be made?␀␀you aim the camera, then tap.␀␀␀12 new seed words, made on this signer␀␀this samples 3 words. the full check comes after the passphrase.␀␀␀␀3-WORD SPOT CHECK␀␀␀this signer takes an encrypted backup:
